You build a Flow Designer flow to create a follow-up task for every new P2 incident and link it back to the incident. The flow steps are exported below.

```json
{
  "trigger": {
    "table": "incident",
    "when": "record_created",
    "conditions": [
      {"field": "priority", "operator": "=", "value": "2"}
    ]
  },
  "steps": [
    {
      "action": "Create Record",
      "table": "sc_task",
      "fields": {
        "parent": "${Trigger -> Record}",
        "short_description": "Follow-up on P2 incident",
        "assignment_group": "Service Desk"
      },
      "outputs_alias": "CreatedTask"
    },
    {
      "action": "Update Record",
      "record": "${Trigger -> Record}",
      "fields": {
        "u_followup_task": "${CreatedTask -> Record.sys_id}"
      }
    }
  ]
}
```
After the flow runs on INC0010001, which record has `u_followup_task` populated and with what value?

A developer adds this onSubmit Client Script to the Incident form:

```javascript
function onSubmit() {
  var gr = new GlideRecord('incident');
  gr.addQuery('number', g_form.getValue('number'));
  gr.query();
  if (!gr.next()) {
    alert('Record not found');
    return false;
  }
}
```
