An onChange Client Script tries to derive a department from the selected caller using a synchronous GlideAjax call:

```javascript
function onChange(control, oldValue, newValue, isLoading) {
  if (isLoading || newValue === '') return;
  var ga = new GlideAjax('UserInfo');
  ga.addParam('sysparm_name', 'getDept');
  ga.addParam('sysparm_user', newValue);
  var response = ga.getXMLWait();
  var dept = response.responseXML.documentElement.getAttribute('dept');
  g_form.setValue('u_department_name', dept);
}
```
Users rapidly change the Caller field several times. What impact will this pattern have?

An outbound REST integration uses this Scripted RESTMessageV2 call:

```javascript
var r = new sn_ws.RESTMessageV2('x_acme_ext', 'create');
r.setRequestBody(JSON.stringify({ name: 'Alpha' }));
// no Content-Type header set
var resp = r.execute();
gs.info('Status: ' + resp.getStatusCode());
```
The external API requires JSON with Content-Type application/json. What response is most likely from the external server?

A Client Script calls a Script Include via GlideAjax:

```javascript
// Client
var ga = new GlideAjax('UserInfo');
ga.addParam('sysparm_name','getDept');
ga.getXMLAnswer(function(ans){ g_form.setValue('u_dept', ans); });
```
The Script Include is defined as:

```javascript
var UserInfo = Class.create();
UserInfo.prototype = {
  initialize: function() {},
  getDept: function() { return 'Finance'; },
  type: 'UserInfo'
};
```
The Script Include is not marked "Client callable" and does not extend AbstractAjaxProcessor. What happens when the client calls it?

scenario_questions.scenario:
A team added an outbound integration that posts updates to a third-party system whenever an Incident’s state changes. They implemented it in a synchronous before update Business Rule on incident:

```javascript
(function executeRule(current, previous /*null when async*/ ) {
  if (!current.state.changes()) return;
  var r = new sn_ws.RESTMessageV2('x_acme_thirdparty','post_update');
  r.setRequestBody(JSON.stringify({
    number: current.number.toString(),
    state: current.state.getDisplayValue(),
    updated_by: gs.getUserName()
  }));
  var resp = r.execute();
  if (resp.getStatusCode() == 200) {
    current.u_synced = true;
    current.update(); // ensure flag persists
  }
})(current, previous);
```
Shortly after deployment, users report intermittent duplicate updates being posted and occasional errors: "Rule recursion detected" and slowness on form save.
